1
00:00:16,183 --> 00:00:18,101
Why do you keep playing with that?

2
00:00:18,936 --> 00:00:20,736
Because I'm skeptical.

3
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:22,655
Do you think this really works?

4
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:25,908
Oh, it's just about making
the candidate seem familiar,

5
00:00:25,943 --> 00:00:28,243
so that the voter sees herself in him.

6
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:30,823
But... you've gone too far.

7
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,159
There.

8
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:37,913
Congratulations,
Francis. You have my vote.

9
00:00:39,081 --> 00:00:42,125
- When do you leave for New York?
- Now.

10
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:46,303
- Then I'm back for the event with Cathy.
- Mmm.

11
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:48,548
It's very risky, what Macallan is doing.

12
00:00:51,093 --> 00:00:53,303
Do you think it's worth it?

13
00:02:33,261 --> 00:02:37,565
- <font color="#D81D1D">Synced and corrected by VitoSilans</font> -
-- <font color="#138CE9">www.Addic7ed.com</font> --

14
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:54,172
- Danton and Sharp just lawyered up.
- They don't want to testify?

15
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,631
And there's no way subpoenas get them

16
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:57,209
in front of the committee
before the election.

17
00:02:57,211 --> 00:02:59,886
There's a rumor the committee's trying
to make a deal with Garrett Walker.

18
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:03,065
No, Walker doesn't want
to do damage to the party.

19
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,858
So why did Jim Matthews agree to appear?

20
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,985
I'm already getting pummeled
with questions about it.

21
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:10,155
- Does he have anything to say?
- Uh, even if he pleads the Fifth,

22
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,484
they get a perp walk that
implicates the president.

23
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:16,154
I didn't know anyone actually ate those.

24
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,907
I look forward to this stuff all year.

25
00:03:21,076 --> 00:03:23,752
Do we have anything on
the committee members?

26
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:25,705
Nothing too juicy yet, I'm afraid.

27
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,673
Vice chairman had an affair
with a young male staffer

28
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:31,927
before he came out
to his wife. Old news.

29
00:03:31,962 --> 00:03:36,049
Committee chairman's squeaky clean
other than a minor back-tax issue.

30
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:39,935
I did find some revenge porn on
the chairman's chief of staff,

31
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:42,479
but I don't think it's worth much.

32
00:03:42,514 --> 00:03:43,939
Is it enough to scare her?

33
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:48,736
Embarrass her, probably.
More than that, probably not.

34
00:04:00,991 --> 00:04:03,699
I gotta say, they look a lot
better on you, Mrs. Underwood,

35
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:05,335
than they would on Governor Conway.

36
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:09,172
Maybe that's why he
didn't wanna pay for it.

37
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:15,303
These masks will be distributed
to all MTA engineers,

38
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:17,680
conductors and maintenance workers.

39
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:21,559
And this model is highly effective
in case of a chemical attack.

40
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:24,021
And I believe Mayor Adalardi
would like to say a few words.

41
00:04:24,056 --> 00:04:25,182
Absolutely.

42
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:30,652
Safety in all branches of the
public transportation system

43
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:32,529
- is my number one priority.
- Ken?

44
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:36,401
- That means subways, that means buses...
- It's fine, I know him.

45
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:38,660
What are you doing here?

46
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:41,246
- What? This is my stop.
- Oh.

47
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,832
- Well, you look well.
- Well, I can't complain.

48
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:48,879
Can't complain, except... Well,
I'm sure you heard about Tim.

49
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:50,380
Corbet? No.

50
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:53,759
- Beth didn't call?
- No.

51
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:56,929
Oh, man. I hate to be
the one to tell you this.

52
00:04:56,964 --> 00:05:02,344
Tim went out on the Arkansas River.
He's been missing for two days now.

53
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:06,063
I thought for sure the
president would have heard.

54
00:05:06,098 --> 00:05:08,606
I mean, I can't imagine
how Frank's gonna take this.

55
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:11,193
Oh, my goodness! Beth and the
kids must be so distraught.

56
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:15,023
Sure. But Frank and Tim's
relationship was special.

57
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,785
It's great to see you, Claire.

58
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:22,245
Would you ask Frank to give me a call?

59
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,867
- Mrs. Underwood?
- Uh, just one moment.

60
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:31,539
See that gentleman I was speaking
to? Go ask him to wait for me, please.

61
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:34,542
Governors, we are running out of time.

62
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:39,596
The fact that you are here at this
emergency meeting on such short notice

63
00:05:39,631 --> 00:05:44,601
tells the American people that you are
as concerned about their safety as I am.

64
00:05:44,636 --> 00:05:46,937
Terror is unacceptable.

65
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:48,681
I do not accept it.

66
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:53,360
But we will not be deterred by
Washington's failure to address it.

67
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:58,531
We will work together,
side by side, fighting back.

68
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:02,702
State by state, city by city,
neighborhood by neighborhood.

69
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:09,452
Because, make no mistake... we are
engaged in the battle of our time.

70
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:12,754
The question of what
it is to be an American,

71
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:15,465
the very essence of American-ness,

72
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:20,755
how we choose to lead our lives,
open and free, is on the line.

73
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:24,676
Fear is un-American.

74
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:30,147
And yes, the irony of saying those
words to you on Halloween, of all days,

75
00:06:30,182 --> 00:06:32,274
is not lost on me.

76
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:37,940
But although we may choose, as Americans,
to scare ourselves once a year for fun...

77
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:44,286
no one else tells any American when to
shake in their boots at any other time.

78
00:06:44,321 --> 00:06:47,122
So I am issuing an executive order,

79
00:06:47,157 --> 00:06:51,751
by virtue of the authority vested in
me as President of the United States

80
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:54,212
and commander in chief
of the armed forces.

81
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:57,424
By our Constitution and
the laws of our land,

82
00:06:57,459 --> 00:07:00,885
including Section Blah-Blah
of the Blah-Blah Act

83
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:06,349
and Section Blah-Blah of Title
Blah-Blah, Paragraph Bullshit-Bullshit.

84
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:08,009
In case you have no
idea what's going on,

85
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:10,979
I'm swelling these states'
National Guard troops

86
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:14,607
to create secure public
spaces on Election Day.

87
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:18,361
I'm urging these governors to
consolidate their polling sites

88
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:21,823
and create quote,
unquote "voting centers"

89
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:24,326
so that people feel safe
to come out and vote.

90
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:29,456
I'm commending Governor Sally
Morrison of the great state of Arizona,

91
00:07:29,491 --> 00:07:33,210
for giving us all such a
good example of voting centers

92
00:07:33,245 --> 00:07:35,921
as used in their recent primary.

93
00:07:35,956 --> 00:07:41,634
But what I'm really doing is seducing
the governors of five key states.

94
00:07:41,669 --> 00:07:46,764
New Jersey, Nevada, Illinois,
Ohio and Pennsylvania.

95
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:51,603
Messrs. Harcourt, Nuñez, Gallinard,

96
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:56,066
Olmstead and Matthews.

97
00:07:56,101 --> 00:07:58,318
Oh, you remember Matthews, don't you?

98
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:01,738
Former vice president to
President Garrett Walker.

99
00:08:01,773 --> 00:08:05,610
Nothing but a provincial
and petty pen-stealer.

100
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:10,372
But I need him.

101
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:14,292
I need all five on my side if
I'm gonna win this election.

102
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:18,838
Matthews, in our history,
he's the biggest known unknown.

103
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:22,300
Oh, and I almost forgot.
The boy wonder is here.

104
00:08:22,335 --> 00:08:27,014
My worthy opponent. Out of
his element and stuck in mine.

105
00:08:27,049 --> 00:08:30,427
But, you see, in politics,
stature is everything.

106
00:08:31,469 --> 00:08:35,807
And wouldn't you say that Willy C
is getting shorter by the minute?

107
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:41,194
These border restrictions
the president is proposing...

108
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:44,031
should the military play a
role in enforcing them, General?

109
00:08:44,066 --> 00:08:45,615
I think we need to take a step back

110
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,201
and look at our national
security priorities.

111
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:52,330
And what constitutes appropriate
deployment of our serving men and women.

112
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:56,668
As veterans, this issue is a personal
one for Governor Conway and me.

113
00:08:56,703 --> 00:08:58,369
- Would you and...
- I'll tell you something else.

114
00:08:58,371 --> 00:08:59,870
You won't hear this from
the governor himself,

115
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:04,426
but his military career is distinguished
by exceptional acts of bravery.

116
00:09:04,461 --> 00:09:09,222
In particular, the incident for which he
was awarded the Purple Heart stands out.

117
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:12,059
Speaks to the kind of
commander in chief he will be.

118
00:09:12,094 --> 00:09:15,187
Demonstrates what I
call fearless wisdom.

119
00:09:15,222 --> 00:09:18,065
Someday soon, America needs to
hear the full story of that day.

120
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,400
Thank you for your
time, General Brockhart.

121
00:09:20,435 --> 00:09:21,526
Glad to talk to you.

122
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,736
Coming up next on Special
Report, we take a look at...

123
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:26,739
I swear to God, if Underwood
puts soldiers on those borders,

124
00:09:26,774 --> 00:09:29,326
I'll be the first to
tell them not to listen.

125
00:09:30,612 --> 00:09:32,704
In terms of allocation of funds,

126
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:35,248
it's our water supply
that keeps me up at night.

127
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:38,168
Roger, are you talking about
protecting the infrastructure?

128
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:40,128
Infrastructure and water sources.

129
00:09:40,163 --> 00:09:43,340
Reservoirs, the dams, the
tunnel delivery systems...

130
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:44,466
All of it, yes.

131
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:48,553
Protection from terrorism, sure, but
the voters see even greater dangers.

132
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,805
Structural, environmental,
toxins from algae.

133
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,307
Algae's quite a problem for us.

134
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:55,852
The big question here, are
the feds doing all they can do?

135
00:09:55,887 --> 00:09:57,479
Well, the feds want to do even more.

136
00:09:57,514 --> 00:09:59,347
That's the reason that
we're all meeting here today.

137
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:00,857
Now, look, gentlemen, all I can see

138
00:10:00,892 --> 00:10:02,767
is that we're in violent
agreement with each other.

139
00:10:02,769 --> 00:10:04,902
I mean, Roger, how long
have we known each other?

140
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:06,154
How far do we go back?

141
00:10:06,189 --> 00:10:08,030
You knew me when I had
hair, Mr. President.

142
00:10:09,151 --> 00:10:11,276
It doesn't change the fact
that my constituents are saying,

143
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:13,078
"Give me a bridge, not a war zone."

144
00:10:13,113 --> 00:10:14,079
All I'm saying is that

145
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:16,748
we need to anticipate threats
when we can and thwart them.

146
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:18,791
I'm saying that we're
days away from an election,

147
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:22,330
- and I don't wanna upset the apple cart.
- Excuse me for just a moment.

148
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:26,042
Will, have you seen this?

149
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:31,088
All right. I'll deal with him later.

150
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:36,511
- Tell me exactly what she said.
- Just that she heard it from Ken Caswell.

151
00:10:41,266 --> 00:10:44,567
I checked with the local
authorities in Salida, sir.

152
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:46,271
It doesn't look good.

153
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:49,447
- The chances of...
- Amp up the search.

154
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:53,326
Whatever materials and personnel they need
in addition to what they have, give them.

155
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:56,204
And reach out to Beth Corbet.
I'd like to speak to her directly.

156
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:57,699
Yes, sir.

157
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:05,338
I haven't slept a good
night's sleep since 2012.

158
00:11:05,373 --> 00:11:09,669
But I guess elected officials
don't sleep so our constituents can.

159
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:13,005
The proof of success
in fighting terror...

160
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:16,050
is something the public
never hears about.

161
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:21,180
A certain city in my state wears
the biggest target in the nation.

162
00:11:22,432 --> 00:11:24,857
The city and state of New York...

163
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:27,937
has scored silent wins for 15 years...

164
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:30,732
without a declaration of war.

165
00:11:32,234 --> 00:11:33,235
Now...

166
00:11:34,277 --> 00:11:35,528
in most cases...

167
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:39,581
I would argue the states
can take care of themselves.

168
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:42,834
- Mr. President!
- Well, by all means, continue, Governor.

169
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:45,913
What... what was that part you
were talking about? Insomnia?

170
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:48,130
My point is,

171
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:51,718
we're all Americans in this room,
and we all love this country.

172
00:11:51,753 --> 00:11:53,177
And I'd like to thank the president

173
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:56,681
for the opportunity to discuss
this very important topic,

174
00:11:56,716 --> 00:12:00,477
and apologize for, uh, being
on such a tight schedule.

175
00:12:00,512 --> 00:12:02,186
Well, we are enormously grateful

176
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:05,315
that the governor took the
time to come and join us today.

177
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:08,485
I'm just trying to understand.

178
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:13,072
Claire, if I said anything to
offend you, it was entirely...

179
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:16,200
I mean, you know me. No filter.

180
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:18,160
And that's what worries me.

181
00:12:18,195 --> 00:12:21,205
I'm just operating on instinct, Ken.

182
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:25,877
- Did you come down here with an agenda?
- No. I mean...

183
00:12:25,912 --> 00:12:28,921
I have been trying to reach
Frank, but today was just...

184
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:32,925
I saw that you were appearing at
an event and I showed up to say hi.

185
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:36,804
I... I really do work around here,
on a street called "Wall," you know?

186
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:40,016
But then you made reference to
something about two very close friends

187
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:42,720
that's nobody's
business, including yours.

188
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:47,767
And you even said so yourself, Ken,
that you have an awfully big mouth.

189
00:12:48,810 --> 00:12:49,811
I...

190
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,820
I lost a dear friend.

191
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,448
I loved Tim. Everybody did.

192
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:58,660
And you implied Francis especially.

193
00:12:58,695 --> 00:13:01,788
Well, yeah. I mean... That
was a whole other thing.

194
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:02,782
In what way?

195
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:08,002
In... What do you want me to say?

196
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:10,915
I'm sure I don't know
anything you don't.

197
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:15,009
I'm just very interested
in your perspective.

198
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:19,424
Frank worshipped Tim, would
have done anything for him.

199
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,892
I don't know.

200
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:27,098
If the world were a different
place back then... who knows?

201
00:13:30,602 --> 00:13:35,279
That was a long time
ago. And then he met you.

202
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,733
And lucky him.

203
00:13:38,109 --> 00:13:42,203
Look, in terms of my firm and... and
trying to get the president's ear...

204
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,789
I mean, yeah, it's a little embarrassing

205
00:13:44,824 --> 00:13:49,454
that my friend of 30-whatever years
didn't have time to pick up the phone.

206
00:13:52,499 --> 00:13:54,333
He should have called you back.

207
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:59,213
Francis and Tim were very good friends.

208
00:14:00,882 --> 00:14:06,888
But, you know, Ken, the older I get,
I learn that assumptions are dangerous.

209
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,642
Sure. Okay.

210
00:14:12,935 --> 00:14:14,353
It was great to see you.

211
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,847
So where is she?

212
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:45,885
Change of plans. She
needed to stay in New York.

213
00:14:46,928 --> 00:14:49,103
She asked me to put
something together for this.

214
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,522
Yeah? Well, something came up.

215
00:14:50,557 --> 00:14:52,357
The vice president will
be filling in for her.

216
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,363
Oh, my...

217
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,149
- Hey, man.
- Hey.

218
00:15:00,942 --> 00:15:05,036
Uh, we played in a terrible
band together back in the day.

219
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:08,491
Before adulthood and
alimony came crashing down.

220
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:12,704
- Two exes? Wow.
- Mmm. Mmm-hmm.

221
00:15:13,705 --> 00:15:16,040
So, uh, where's the First Lady?

222
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:19,467
- Something came up.
- Hmm.

223
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:22,804
I'd love to ask you a few questions
about working on the campaign.

224
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:24,389
I'm just a speechwriter.

225
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:26,549
Exactly. How the hell did that happen?

226
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:28,851
Welcome to the Council
on Foreign Relations

227
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:32,640
and this special event on
Crossing Borders: The Way Forward.

228
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:37,437
I smell a swing state party.

229
00:15:39,439 --> 00:15:41,280
Tone, Rick.

230
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:44,742
You didn't have to round up dozens of
governors just to talk to the five of us.

231
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:47,328
You're here because there
have been concerning threats

232
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,581
in exurban counties
in each of your states.

233
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:51,332
Could you be more specific?

234
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,919
We're keeping an eye on Hunterdon,
Elko, Jefferson counties.

235
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,797
Also Chester and McHenry.

236
00:15:57,832 --> 00:16:00,675
Which is why it's crucial that we
work with your states' administrations

237
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:02,719
