477
00:31:27,428 --> 00:31:28,845
My events went well.

478
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:36,269
And? What aren't you telling me?

479
00:31:38,522 --> 00:31:41,031
I bumped into Ken Caswell.

480
00:31:41,066 --> 00:31:43,610
- Does he know any more?
- No, um...

481
00:31:44,528 --> 00:31:47,579
- Why didn't you call him back?
- What?

482
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:50,081
His Treasury business.
The oversight legislation.

483
00:31:50,116 --> 00:31:53,043
I understand you don't
care about it. Fine.

484
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:56,707
But you can't ignore loose ends
like that. You owed him your ear.

485
00:31:57,874 --> 00:32:00,592
Well, I didn't realize it
was gonna become so personal.

486
00:32:00,627 --> 00:32:03,336
I am the President of the United States,
for Christ's sake. I'm a bit busy.

487
00:32:03,338 --> 00:32:06,807
The past doesn't disappear
on command, Francis.

488
00:32:06,842 --> 00:32:08,885
Not even for presidents.

489
00:32:09,970 --> 00:32:11,262
What did he say to you?

490
00:32:12,639 --> 00:32:15,350
Ken's got a big mouth.

491
00:32:24,943 --> 00:32:28,905
I'm sorry about Tim.
I'm sorry he's gone.

492
00:32:30,073 --> 00:32:31,950
I know how you felt about him.

493
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:34,495
Or, I can imagine.

494
00:32:35,662 --> 00:32:36,997
Listen to me.

495
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:42,092
You know you're the only
person I've ever truly loved.

496
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:43,795
You know that, right?

497
00:32:55,807 --> 00:32:57,225
And listen.

498
00:32:58,393 --> 00:33:00,687
Something else is about to happen.

499
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:50,696
Welcome back.

500
00:33:51,279 --> 00:33:54,247
Reception is sketchy. Good trip?

501
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:58,286
I just came back to get changed.
I need to get back to Francis.

502
00:34:01,247 --> 00:34:03,083
You mad at me?

503
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:05,627
You shouldn't have said that.

504
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:10,298
I know. I know we need to be careful.

505
00:34:12,676 --> 00:34:16,805
Careful is far too small a
word for what we need to be.

506
00:34:17,513 --> 00:34:18,431
Okay.

507
00:34:22,603 --> 00:34:26,231
But don't you get tired of being
far bigger than careful all the time?

508
00:34:29,188 --> 00:34:31,651
- I don't know what's going on.
- Me neither.

509
00:34:31,653 --> 00:34:33,995
Seems to be some kind
of network disturbance.

510
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,711
I lost connection on my server.

511
00:35:02,851 --> 00:35:07,195
You know what I'm tired
of? This role. First Lady.

512
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:09,024
'Cause it's never felt right.

513
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:13,034
It's only eight more days
to the vice presidency.

514
00:35:13,069 --> 00:35:16,489
- Mmm-hmm. What's my role?
- What?

515
00:35:17,699 --> 00:35:21,411
What am I to you, anyway? Or you, to me?

516
00:35:23,038 --> 00:35:24,665
I mean, are you my girlfriend?

517
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:27,250
And when you win...

518
00:35:28,168 --> 00:35:31,630
does that make me,
like, First Boyfriend?

519
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:34,841
First Concubine?

520
00:35:39,054 --> 00:35:41,597
About that article... I'm sorry.

521
00:35:42,515 --> 00:35:44,184
I hate apologies.

522
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:51,858
I'm sorry.

523
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:02,786
I looked over at you.
I watched you watching.

524
00:36:05,997 --> 00:36:09,299
- When?
- Did it even affect you?

525
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:10,794
The beheading?

526
00:36:12,212 --> 00:36:15,841
- Why would you ask that?
- I had no sense of what you were thinking.

527
00:36:16,758 --> 00:36:17,843
None.

528
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,644
Of what I was thinking?
I wasn't thinking.

529
00:36:20,679 --> 00:36:22,597
I was thinking, "Don't think."

530
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:31,773
And I'll tell you something else.
I never said I like being careful.

531
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:38,203
- God damn it.
- What's wrong?

532
00:36:38,238 --> 00:36:40,997
The GPS thinks we're
back at the White House.

533
00:36:41,032 --> 00:36:45,043
- Did you reach the campaign office?
- Trying. I can't get a signal.

534
00:36:45,078 --> 00:36:46,788
Oh, wait. Here we go.

535
00:36:48,289 --> 00:36:49,840
I can't miss this flight.

536
00:36:49,875 --> 00:36:52,543
- It's ringing.
- Good.

537
00:36:53,628 --> 00:36:55,428
- How long do you think?
- Now it stopped.

538
00:36:55,463 --> 00:36:58,299
There's a pile-up on the
highway. I'm doing the best I can.

539
00:37:03,388 --> 00:37:04,555
Hello?

540
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:07,607
Hello!

541
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:11,945
- Tanya, let me try your phone.
- I'm having the same issues.

542
00:37:11,980 --> 00:37:15,198
- Can you get through to the office?
- No, Governor, I can't.

543
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:17,408
Garrett is a good man.

544
00:37:17,443 --> 00:37:20,411
- A trustworthy man?
- Absolutely, Mr. Romero.

545
00:37:20,446 --> 00:37:21,788
And is he the kind of man

546
00:37:21,823 --> 00:37:24,540
who would knowingly participate
in campaign finance fraud?

547
00:37:24,575 --> 00:37:26,369
I wouldn't say that, exactly. No.

548
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:29,039
How well do you know
President Underwood, sir?

549
00:37:29,790 --> 00:37:32,132
I've known the president four years.

550
00:37:32,167 --> 00:37:34,134
Isn't it a fact that
it was Francis Underwood

551
00:37:34,169 --> 00:37:36,797
and not President Walker who
first suggested you should resign?

552
00:37:41,509 --> 00:37:43,845
To the best of my recollection, no.

553
00:37:44,595 --> 00:37:47,188
And isn't it true that the source
of campaign funds you received

554
00:37:47,223 --> 00:37:48,722
as the president's
running mate was connected

555
00:37:48,724 --> 00:37:52,353
to a pay-for-play scheme that reached
all the way from Missouri to China?

556
00:37:53,313 --> 00:37:55,530
To the best of my knowledge, no.

557
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:59,861
Did you receive any campaign donations
through Raymond Tusk's firm, Clayton West?

558
00:38:00,821 --> 00:38:02,746
Not to the best of my recollection.

559
00:38:02,781 --> 00:38:03,863
Do you think your recollection

560
00:38:03,865 --> 00:38:05,665
or knowledge will improve
as the day goes on?

561
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:07,042
Excuse me?

562
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:19,505
Beth.

563
00:38:20,966 --> 00:38:23,141
I want you to promise
me that you'll call me

564
00:38:23,176 --> 00:38:25,220
anytime you need anything.

565
00:38:26,930 --> 00:38:29,390
You were the love of
Tim's life, you know that.

566
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:34,104
Well, I should probably...

567
00:38:36,940 --> 00:38:38,524
Yes. You, too.

568
00:38:40,193 --> 00:38:41,569
Goodbye.

569
00:38:44,614 --> 00:38:46,039
Thank you, Felix.

570
00:38:46,074 --> 00:38:48,083
Uh, would you like me to
prepare it for you, sir?

571
00:38:48,118 --> 00:38:50,036
No, I'll be fine. Thank you.

572
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:16,236
The first question to ask
yourself... "Is the damper open?"

573
00:39:16,271 --> 00:39:19,948
Never allow yourself to
be overcome with smoke.

574
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:23,576
Conflagration relies on airflow.
That's what the grate is for.

575
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:26,454
Now, I like a one-inch base of ash.

576
00:39:26,489 --> 00:39:30,291
It's helpful, but of course they clean
up around here too soon to do that.

577
00:39:30,326 --> 00:39:35,005
Now, as for the architecture of the
logs, I prefer the upside-down method.

578
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:38,508
Largest logs right along the base.

579
00:39:38,543 --> 00:39:41,504
Then medium-size logs after that.

580
00:39:45,508 --> 00:39:47,218
Small logs.

581
00:39:51,264 --> 00:39:54,350
And then finally, kindling...

582
00:39:56,477 --> 00:39:57,777
and tinder.

583
00:39:57,812 --> 00:40:01,447
Now, of course, back home,
dead palmetto fronds are ideal.

584
00:40:01,482 --> 00:40:03,324
But, of course, here in Washington,

585
00:40:03,359 --> 00:40:06,446
we have to use whatever
garbage we find lying around.

586
00:40:07,488 --> 00:40:12,327
But then, if a man cannot
use what's right in...

587
00:40:17,748 --> 00:40:19,542
God damn it, Tim.

588
00:40:26,674 --> 00:40:30,894
If a man is not smart enough to be
able to use whatever is in front of him

589
00:40:30,929 --> 00:40:32,888
and still make it work...

590
00:40:33,974 --> 00:40:39,062
well, then... that's just
a failure of the imagination.

591
00:40:56,412 --> 00:40:59,047
right here. And I'm thinking...

592
00:40:59,082 --> 00:41:00,840
"Wait, do I tell him? Do..."

593
00:41:00,875 --> 00:41:03,086
Uh, I gotta take this.

594
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:05,220
Hey.

595
00:41:05,255 --> 00:41:06,935
Your testimony can't be private.

596
00:41:08,133 --> 00:41:11,017
- I'm sorry to hear that.
- Just wanted to let you know.

597
00:41:20,186 --> 00:41:23,481
What's a "flash blood warning"?
It's coming up on everybody's phones.

598
00:41:25,525 --> 00:41:26,859
Thanks for the drinks.

599
00:42:23,416 --> 00:42:26,551
Tom, stop. No. I... I have to get back.

600
00:42:26,586 --> 00:42:28,003
Come on.

601
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:31,132
No.

602
00:42:32,050 --> 00:42:34,017
Tom!

603
00:42:46,606 --> 00:42:48,858
And, finally, you strike your match...

604
00:42:49,734 --> 00:42:51,444
you ignite your kindling...

605
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:01,794
and then you blow.

606
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:12,132
It's happening, sir.

607
00:43:19,061 --> 00:43:20,904
Citizens should be advised,

608
00:43:20,907 --> 00:43:23,274
a wave of disruptions
is currently affecting

609
00:43:23,309 --> 00:43:26,152
Internet and cellular
service in the DC area.

610
00:43:26,187 --> 00:43:27,737
Expect traffic and travel delays

611
00:43:27,772 --> 00:43:31,699
as authorities are still trying to
determine the scope of the problem.

612
00:43:31,734 --> 00:43:34,410
- Are we gonna make this flight?
- I don't know.

613
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:36,079
Unconfirmed reports speculate

614
00:43:36,114 --> 00:43:38,623
the disruptions may be
connected to a cyber-attack

615
00:43:38,658 --> 00:43:39,957
with possible ties to ICO.

616
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:42,293
- My God.
- What?

617
00:43:42,328 --> 00:43:43,336
Maybe they were right.

618
00:43:43,371 --> 00:43:45,329
Maybe we should have said yes
to the offer of those troops.

619
00:43:45,331 --> 00:43:48,674
National Guard on patrol makes us look
weak right before an election. Forget it.

620
00:43:48,709 --> 00:43:50,753
- But, Governor...
- I made my decision, Tanya.

621
00:44:35,923 --> 00:44:37,132
Not yet.

622
00:44:44,182 --> 00:44:47,150
They're patching through the
heads of all the carriers, sir.

623
00:44:47,185 --> 00:44:50,945
Gentlemen and ladies, can you hear me?

624
00:44:50,980 --> 00:44:52,322
Yes, Mr. President.

625
00:44:52,357 --> 00:44:55,658
Good. Then tell me how in
God's name this has happened.

626
00:44:55,693 --> 00:44:58,869
Uh, we don't know yet, sir. We're
still working on the problem.

627
00:44:58,904 --> 00:45:01,824
We're reaching out to
as many people as we...

628
00:45:03,659 --> 00:45:05,035
Did we just lose them?

629
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:07,587
Is this a joke?

630
00:46:08,474 --> 00:46:11,101
The Ohio governor is
calling from a payphone.

631
00:46:16,982 --> 00:46:18,658
This is the president.

632
00:46:18,693 --> 00:46:20,618
Mr. President, I've changed my mind.

633
00:46:20,653 --> 00:46:21,994
If the offer's still open,

634
00:46:22,029 --> 00:46:25,039
I'd like to accept additional
troops for the state of Ohio.

635
00:46:25,074 --> 00:46:27,868
Just say the word,
Roger. Whatever you need.

636
00:46:31,205 --> 00:46:34,965
My fellow Americans,
the facts are these.

637
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:38,260
The greater District of Columbia
area and the immediate region beyond

638
00:46:38,295 --> 00:46:41,847
have undergone what we suspect
is an ICO-sponsored cyber-attack.

639
00:46:41,882 --> 00:46:45,768
The attack was aimed at the district's
main telecom switching center.

640
00:46:45,803 --> 00:46:47,219
In addition to intermittent outages,

641
00:46:47,221 --> 00:46:49,980
a considerable amount of
havoc has been wreaked.

642
00:46:50,015 --> 00:46:54,234
Traffic lights have been disabled.
One area train has been derailed.

643
00:46:54,269 --> 00:46:57,613
The system that maintains our
sewers has been tampered with.

644
00:46:57,648 --> 00:46:59,865
The perpetrators were
targeting the government

645
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:01,992
and their ultimate
purpose, though foiled,

646
00:47:02,027 --> 00:47:05,913
was to disrupt all mid-Atlantic
transportation networks.

647
00:47:05,948 --> 00:47:09,667
Events like these underscore the
urgency of my request to Congress

648
00:47:09,702 --> 00:47:11,502
for a declaration of war.

649
00:47:11,537 --> 00:47:15,631
Tonight, I can only suspect Congress
will spend a dark night of the soul,

650
00:47:15,666 --> 00:47:19,927
after which they will reconsider
their paralysis and choose to act.

651
00:47:19,962 --> 00:47:21,596
Capital East Telecom has informed me

652
00:47:21,631 --> 00:47:24,098
that it's repairing the
network as fast as possible,

653
00:47:24,133 --> 00:47:27,810
but that it will take at least a
couple more days to be fully restored.

654
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:30,480
It is an unfortunate but undeniable fact

655
00:47:30,515 --> 00:47:33,608
that we will continue to
experience attacks until ICO

656
00:47:33,643 --> 00:47:38,195
and other terrorist groups like it
are eliminated swiftly and completely.

657
00:47:38,230 --> 00:47:40,698
Thank you. May God bless you.

658
00:47:40,733 --> 00:47:43,235
And may God bless the
United States of America.

659
00:47:50,200 --> 00:47:51,285
We off?

660
00:47:59,502 --> 00:48:01,421
- Good evening, Ted.
- Hi, Hannah.

661
00:48:03,297 --> 00:48:04,764
I saw your interview.

662
00:48:04,799 --> 00:48:08,768
I'd appreciate it if you didn't bring
up the details of my combat record.

663
00:48:08,803 --> 00:48:11,514
You were a hero that day.
You should use it, Will.

664
00:48:18,187 --> 00:48:19,437
Governor, aren't you worried about

665
00:48:19,439 --> 00:48:22,281
bringing your kids out in the
middle of a terrorist attack?

666
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:26,827
It'd be scarier to keep the kids at
home. The streets are safe. Life goes on.

667
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:32,409
You've got to be kidding me.

668
00:48:37,206 --> 00:48:39,083
What's on your mind, Governor?

669
00:48:43,378 --> 00:48:46,466
What's on my mind? I mean,
you see what's going on here.

670
00:48:47,216 --> 00:48:50,309
This is all him. It's a
man who's never served.

671
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:53,178
Wouldn't know what a real war was if
it jumped up and bit him in the ass.

672
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:54,849
I mean, a declaration of war?

673
00:48:55,766 --> 00:48:58,102
He's putting American lives in danger.

674
00:48:59,311 --> 00:49:01,028
- War is real!
- Nightcap?

675
00:49:01,063 --> 00:49:04,108
- You don't screw around with it.
- Why not?

676
00:49:05,485 --> 00:49:07,076
This is what happens.

677
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:09,912
This is what happens when you
throw around a word like "war."

678
00:49:09,947 --> 00:49:11,371
All hell breaks loose.

679
00:49:23,663 --> 00:49:29,383
